# Why This Table Exists

Rather than storing source information repeatedly for every applicant, each application references a single source record. This improves data consistency, reduces duplication, and makes it possible to analyze recruitment performance across different channels.

Example questions this table helps answer:

- Which recruitment source generates the most applications?
- Which partners produce the highest acceptance rate?
- Which channels generate the highest-quality candidates?
- Which regions contribute the most successful applicants